{"agent":"main","body":{"args_hash":"sha256:2b796593171862ab6ba195a8f1350927f42126f07f2b98a8b0ac6261c1535c14","args_inline":{"content":"---\nname: project-fx-convert-rounding\ndescription: ledger.fx.convert used int() truncation causing cumulative rounding drift on FX-converted accounts\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`ledger/fx.py`'s `convert(cents, rate)` used `int(cents * rate)`, which truncates toward zero instead of rounding to the nearest cent. Over ~3200 transactions this created a systematic downward bias, surfacing as account 4471 (the only EUR-denominated account, \"EU Receivables\") being off by 0.30 EUR against `fixtures/controls.csv` while all USD accounts matched (USD accounts never hit the conversion path since `Rates.get` short-circuits when src==dst).\n\n**Why:** Truncation is a directional bias (always rounds down for positive amounts), so it accumulates across many small conversions rather than averaging out like proper rounding would.\n\n**How to apply:** Fixed by changing to `round(cents * rate)`. If similar reconcile mismatches appear on other FX-touched accounts in this repo, check `ledger/fx.py` and `ledger/rates.py` first — accounts whose currency matches the transaction currency will never show the bug since no conversion occurs.\n","file_path":"/var/folders/yb/b_617z_s2ml933nmr_k7m47m0000gn/T/saga-bench-2671409271/py-0010-ledger-fx-rounding/1/cfg/claude-config/projects/-private-var-folders-yb-b-617z-s2ml933nmr-k7m47m0000gn-T-saga-bench-2671409271-py-0010-ledger-fx-rounding-1-ws/memory/project_fx_convert_rounding.md"},"component":"harness","cwd_rel":".","index_version":null,"tool":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CYba94fy2rcyLYpL4N7ysG"},"hash":"sha256:aa2b3a4a0359e7102385ae6ae0016955c0b83df3c5f72578950499c0a856b8fc","mono_ns":31000000,"prev":"sha256:23cff3e8698416c1fd46e92dda6383c4291226688289ef7b75b425ceb8e19860","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":31,"session":"8ee0ac58-5755-429c-b8a7-c806912171d3","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00: